From: microvm <microvm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x86/alternatives: don't rewrite unchanged text at boot

text_poke_early() writes every site it is handed, then serializes the CPU
with sync_core(). At boot many of those writes put back the bytes already
there: alternatives that aren't applied and have no NOPs to merge. Compare
first and return if nothing changes. The text page then stays clean too,
which keeps it shareable when the kernel image is mapped copy-on-write.

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c	2026-11-04 08:36:06.254343186 +0100
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c	2026-11-04 08:36:06.290121121 +0100
@@ -2534,6 +2534,14 @@
 {
 	unsigned long flags;
 
+	/*
+	 * Many sites keep their bytes: an alternative that isn't applied and
+	 * has no NOPs to merge, a call that stays a call. Writing them anyway
+	 * costs a serializing sync_core() each and dirties the text page.
+	 */
+	if (!memcmp(addr, opcode, len))
+		return;
+
 	if (boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_NX) &&
 	    is_module_text_address((unsigned long)addr)) {
 		/*
